docs/design.md
The files in the orchestrator/ directory are:                                   

 1 bench_local30_gen.py                                                         
 2 bench_local30_grade.py                                                       

The bench_local30_gen.py script performs a local benchmark by generating        
candidates using the Qwen3-Coder-30B model via Ollama's OpenAI-compatible       
endpoint. It:                                                                   

 • Uses the hard-30 query set from eval_queryset_hard.py                        
 • Generates responses for each query using http_call()                         
 • Saves results to eval_candidates_local30_hard.json                           
 • Supports resuming from partial runs                                          
 • Includes a demo mode for offline testing                                     

The bench_local30_grade.py script then grades these local 30B candidates against
the H200-served 80B candidates:                                                 

 • Merges the two answer sets into pairs                                        
 • Uses the same gpt-5.2 grader to score both models on the same queries        
 • Computes win/loss/tie statistics between the models                          
 • Produces a report comparing the local 30B vs the H200 80B performance        

Both scripts are designed to measure whether the local 30B model can serve as a 
viable daily driver replacement for the more expensive H200-served 80B model.   

